	"title"		"Production Limit Profiles"
	"description"		"[b]Set all your production limits with one click.[/b]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]A profile list beside the Production Limits window: Initial, Midgame, Advanced, No limits
[*]Initial, Midgame and Advanced are complete setups for the stages of a colony; No limits clears everything
[*]Make your own profiles, or replace or remove the built-in ones, in a text file (see below)
[*]Uses the window's own limit buttons, so nothing is patched and saves stay normal
[*]Can be switched off under Settings - Mods
[*]Works while paused, and does nothing in the background
[/list]

[h2]Your own profiles[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Create the folder %localappdata%\Whiskerwood\Saved\mods\ProductionLimitsConfig
[*]Save a text file named ProductionLimits.txt there (not ProductionLimits.txt.txt)
[*]Write a [Profile name] line, then one  what = limit  per line
[*]Load your save
[/olist]
[code]
[Farm only]       ; a new button
* = off           ; clear every limit first
wheat = 200
@rawFood = 2500   ; a whole category

[Initial]         ; same name as a built-in: replaces it
* = off
berries = 2500

[Advanced]        ; nothing under it: removes that button
[/code]
[list]
[*][b]what[/b]: a resource id (wood, planks, copperore ...), @category (@rawFood, @ore, @refined, @tools ...) or * for everything
[*][b]limit[/b]: a number (0 allowed), or off for no limit
[*]A profile changes only what it lists; start it with * = off to make it a complete setup
[*]Lines apply top to bottom, a later line wins: @ore = 100 then goldore = off
[*]; or # starts a comment; case and spaces don't matter
[/list]
The full list of resource ids, categories and the built-in profiles (to copy and edit): [url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-productionlimits/blob/main/docs/ProductionLimits-defaults.txt]defaults file on GitHub[/url].

Production limits need an assigned administrator; without one the game ignores the changes.

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/ringuh/whiskerwood-productionlimits]GitHub[/url]

Created using the [url=https://github.com/Whiskerwood-Modding/Whiskerwood-Project]Whiskerwood modkit[/url]."
	"changenote"		"1.0: first release."
}
